ategies, loss control surveys and analysis, consulting, and claims processing services. This segment also offers non-insurance services and products through automobile and recreational vehicle dealer services businesses. It serves commercial, public and quasi-public entities, professionals, and individual customers. The Specialty Distribution segment comprises wholesale brokerage and specialty businesses. This segment offers professional liability and related package insurance products for dentistry, legal, eyecare, financial services, physicians, and real estate title professionals, as well as supplementary insurance products related to weddings, events, medical facilities, and cyber liabilities. This segment also provides public entity-related and specialty programs through a network of independent agents, as well as program management services for insurance carrier partners. In addition, the company's wholesale brokerage businesses underwrite and place excess and surplus commercial and personal lines insurance through independent agents and brokers. Its program businesses operate under the Arrowhead Programs name. The company was formerly known as Poe & Brown, Inc. and changed its name to Brown & Brown, Inc. in April 1999. Brown & Brown, Inc. was founded in 1939 and is headquartered in Daytona Beach, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. J. Powell Brown C.P.C.U. | CEO, President & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $5.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 22K people. Revenue per employee of $258K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 13%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $60K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 22\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Brown & Brown, Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $23.9B market cap on $5.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +18% over the past three years and +14% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 7% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $1.4B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 23 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.38\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.6\u00d7.","Net dilution runs at 16.8% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 13% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Goodwill represents 50% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.12264618916378342},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"100,827 Shares of Brown & Brown, Inc. $BRO Acquired by Mirae Asset Global Investments Co. Ltd.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/100827-shares-of-brown-brown-inc-bro-acquired-by-mirae-asset-global-investments-co-ltd.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793959536.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.927,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Can Brown & Brown (BRO) Keep Looking Like A Bargain?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nyse-bro/brown-brown/news/can-brown-brown-bro-keep-looking-like-a-bargain","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793849957.975,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.893,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Critical Contrast: Chubb (NYSE:CB) vs. Brown & Brown (NYSE:BRO)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/03/critical-contrast-chubb-nysecb-vs-brown-brown-nysebro.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793699963.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.846,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Brown & Brown (BRO) After Earnings And COMPASS Launch Looks Modestly Undervalued","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nyse-bro